{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>The elder of his household.</b> And there is no suspicion of him regarding forbidden relations." "<b>Under my thigh.</b> According to the plain sense it does not refer to circumcision, for if so, he should have sworn by the commandment of circumcision, and behold he swears by the Name, as it is written, 'ואשביעך בה׳'. Rather, such was the custom in those days: every person who was subordinate to another would place his hand under his thigh as a sign — 'you are my lord; behold, my hand is under your authority to do your will.' And this custom still exists today in the land of India." "<b>[Under my thigh.</b> The place of the womb]."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:29.977895077Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}